  "body": {
    "id": "prop:standard-reductions",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "If \\(\\delta_D=\\delta_S=0\\), the branches reduce to no-defier covariate-dependent one-sided selection. If additionally \\(S_0=S_1=1\\) almost surely among compliers, then \\(H=\\sum_xc_x\\) and \\(\\Theta_I\\) reduces to the standard sharp ordinal strict-benefit interval obtained from the complier marginal distributions; for \\(K=2\\), its cellwise numerator inequalities reduce to \\(\\max\\{0,h_x-u_{x1}-v_{x0}\\}\\le n_x\\le\\min\\{h_x,u_{x0},v_{x1}\\}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\delta_D",
      "\\delta_S",
      "S_0",
      "S_1",
      "H",
      "c_x",
      "\\Theta_I",
      "K",
      "h_x",
      "u",
      "v",
      "n_x"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:ordinal-cuts",
      "thm:projection-lifting",
      "thm:attained-connected-endpoints"
    ],
    "justification": "The reductions verify that the joint sensitivity geometry collapses to known no-defier and complete-selection ordinal bounds in standard special cases.",
    "gap": "The special cases are settled by Dong--Heiler and ordinal coupling results; the contribution is the exact interpolation when both monotonicities fail.",
    "consumer": "These reductions provide implementation unit tests and interpretable baseline points for applied sensitivity charts.",
    "proof_tex": "If \\(\\delta_D=0\\), nonnegativity and \\(\\sum_xf_x\\leq0\\) imply \\(f_x=0\\) for every \\(x\\), so every compatible response law has no treatment defiers.  If also \\(\\delta_S=0\\), then\n\\[\n 0\\geq\\sum_x\\min\\{a_x,b_x\\}\\geq0.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\min\\{a_x,b_x\\}=0\\) in every cell: selection is one-sided within each covariate cell, although its direction may vary with \\(x\\).  Conversely, choosing in each cell the zero direction supplies an orientation branch with zero minority left side.  The branches therefore reduce exactly to the no-defier, covariate-dependent one-sided-selection model.\n\nUnder the additional premise that \\(S_0=S_1=1\\) almost surely among compliers, all complier mass is selected under both treatments.  Hence\n\\[\n U_x=V_x=h_x=c_x,\\qquad H=\\sum_xc_x.\n\\]\nThere are no missing complier margins to complete, and the ordinal-cuts lemma says that the attainable numerator is exactly the sharp ordered coupling range generated by the two complier outcome margins.  Projection--lifting proves that these and only these couplings correspond to full compatible laws, while attained connectedness turns their scalar image into the standard sharp interval.\n\nFor \\(K=2\\), the nonbenefit cuts are\n\\[\n B_{x,-1}=U_x,\\qquad B_{x,0}=u_{x1}+v_{x0},\\qquad B_{x,1}=V_x,\n\\]\nand the benefit cuts are\n\\[\n G_{x,0}=v_{x1},\\qquad G_{x,1}=u_{x0},\\qquad G_{x,2}=U_x.\n\\]\nSince \\(h_x\\leq U_x,V_x\\), substitution into the exact cut interval gives\n\\[\n \\max\\{0,h_x-u_{x1}-v_{x0}\\}\n \\leq n_x\\leq\n \\min\\{h_x,u_{x0},v_{x1}\\},\n\\]\nas claimed.",
